    "hammer": {
      "word": "HAMMER",
      "definitions": [
        {
          "text": "An instrument for driving nails, beating metals, and the like, consisting of a head, usually of steel or iron, fixed crosswise to a handle. With busy hammers closing rivets up. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "Something which in firm or action resembles the common hammer; as: (a) That part of a clock which strikes upon the bell to indicate the hour. (b) The padded mallet of a piano, which strikes the wires, to produce the tones. (c) (Anat.) The malleus. See under Ear. (Gun.)",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "That part of a gunlock which strikes the percussion cap, or firing pin; the cock; formerly, however, a piece of steel covering the pan of a flintlock musket and struck by the flint of the cock to ignite the priming. (e) Also, a person of thing that smites or shatters; as, St. Augustine was the hammer of heresies. He met the stern legionaries [of Rome] who had been the \"massive iron hammers\" of the whole earth. J. H. Newman. Atmospheric hammer, a dead-stroke hammer in which the spring is formed by confined air. when cold. bivalve shells, allied to the pearl oysters, having the wings narrow and elongated, so as to give them a hammer-shaped outline; -- called also hammer oyster.",
          "partOfSpeech": "noun"
        },
        {
          "text": "To beat with a hammer; to beat with heavy blows; as, to hammer iron.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To form or forge with a hammer; to shape by beating. \"Hammered money.\" Dryden.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To form in the mind; to shape by hard intellectual labor; -- usually with out. Who was hammering out a penny dialogue. Jeffry.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To be busy forming anything; to labor hard as if shaping something with a hammer. Whereon this month I have hammering. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        },
        {
          "text": "To strike repeated blows, literally or figuratively. Blood and revenge are hammering in my head. Shak.",
          "partOfSpeech": "verb"
        }
      ],
